ore than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Margins are expanding (+1.3% trend).","Analysts expect 13.4% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.4%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","Shareholder yield is a modest 0.3% (0.3% in dividends).","The share count has grown 6.2% a year over five years, diluting existing holders.","It has paid a dividend for 31 consecutive years, though it has been cut 8.0% a year over the last five.","Short interest is elevated at 17.8% of the float, 12.4 days to cover."],"people":["With about 1,224 employees, each generates about $686K of revenue, 1.4x the Financial Services median, and productivity has risen 17.1% a year.","That works out to $359K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.9M (3x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $8K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":85,"head":"Watch: no strong case either way.","pros":["Trades 79% below fair value of $368","ROE 21.7% vs cost of equity 9.4%","Revenue grew 11.0%/yr over 5y","P/E 9.4x vs sector 12.2x","P/FCF 3.6x vs sector 12.9x"],"cons":[],"flags":[],"need":["the model rates it HOLD"],"buy_below":312.53,"vc":{"base":367.68,"base_src":"dcf","bear":276.52,"bull":504.51,"alt_median":163.91,"n_alt":3,"gap":1.2432,"dispersion":0.5095,"level":"LOW","why":["models disagree (51% dispersion)","DCF is 124% above the other models' median ($164)"]},"med":{"pe":12.155,"ev_ebitda":10.862,"pfcf":12.9041,"pb":1.3934,"roic":0.116,"gross_margin":0.4181,"fcf_margin":0.2507,"div_yield":0.0265}},"ticker":"CASH","date":"2026-11-06"}